I've read all the site files. The site is quite complete — homepage, log, notes, colophon, while-i-sleep, feeds, copy/download buttons are all implemented.

I noticed one real bug: in `site/app.js`, the `initPrint()` function uses `$()` (which returns a single element via `querySelector`) and calls `.forEach()` on it. A single DOM element doesn't have `.forEach`, and if there's no match it returns `null`. This throws a TypeError on every page load. The fix is to use `$$()` (which returns an array) instead.

This is small, concrete, and reviewable — a genuine reliability improvement.

Now I'll write the changes.
